## Defects / observations (for the sentinel's end-of-campaign summary)
- **D-1 (script, Test-cases): a "not applicable" step is graded `self.failed` → a full-bench power
  cycle.** TestCase_20 (and similar guards in TestCase_21/30/… that did not fire here) combine
  `self.supported = False` with `self.failed('… case not applicable')`. The framework reports
  UNSUPPORTED but still runs `_power_cycle()`: one six-unit cycle (~4 min) for a case the sweep
  already knew was inapplicable, which is the I-8 pattern again. The fix is the 3454bc0 pattern: a
  DUT property set from the sweep record (e.g. `has_speed_10_and_100`) plus
  `testCasePlatformWithPropertyIncl`/`skipIfExcl`. The sweep only runs inside the TestSet, so an
  equivalent pre-marking has to happen after the sweep, or the case has to log and return without
  `failed()`.
- **D-2 (script, Test-cases): the TestSet tear_down startup-config restore cannot work with
  `--nodefaultcfg`.** At tear_down the framework has set the boot config back to
  `stk_a_9001_33235.cfg`, so `copy <backup> startup-config` is refused (`% Cannot overwrite … as it
  is configured as the boot config file`). The script greps for 'Error'/'Invalid'/… only when taking
  the backup, not here, then deletes the backup anyway. Harmless on tb470 (the tester restores the
  boot pointer), but the restore it claims never happened.
- O-1: IE520 AT-SPTXc copper SFP rejects `speed 10`, and the x230-10GP fixed RJ45 port rejects
  2500/5000/10000. So on this pair, 100 and 1000 are the only fixed speeds (as run 1 found).
- O-2: IE520 AT-SPSX (1000BASE-SX) accepts only `speed 1000` as a fixed speed. 100 and
  10000/40000/100000 are refused with `% … Unsupported speed/duplex combination`, and the
  IE520-sa's SX port refuses the same set. The CLI `speed ?` still offers 10…400000 on the SX port
  (orient §2 "media-blind CLI"), but the refusal happens at execution, so no false "failed to set"
  arises.
- O-3: PDU outlet 5 reads status `'2'` after `on` (the framework's 3-attempt check fails, the 4th
  call succeeds). Second occurrence (2026-09-29 12:55, 2026-10-01 10:42). The unit boots fine.

